# =============================================================
#  admet-gnn / ADMETriage
# =============================================================

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.installed.cfg
.ruff_cache/

# --- Virtual environments ---
venv/
.venv/
.venv-*/
env/
ENV/
#  .venv-*/ catches the throwaway dataset-download environment
#  (.venv-tdc -- see requirements-data.txt). Note that .venv/ does NOT
#  match .venv-tdc/: a trailing-slash pattern matches that exact
#  directory name and nothing else. Every new environment naming scheme
#  needs its own rule, or it turns up as untracked at the worst moment.

# --- Rust ---
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
# Cargo.lock IS committed for binaries -- do not ignore it.

# --- Node / SvelteKit ---
node_modules/
.svelte-kit/
web/build/
web/.vercel/
web/.output/
.pnpm-store/

# --- Tauri ---
desktop/src-tauri/target/
desktop/src-tauri/gen/

# --- Environment / secrets ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
secrets.yaml

# --- Jupyter ---
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Data (large, regenerable -- never commit raw or processed datasets) ---
#  BOTH locations are covered on purpose. Datasets from the MoleculeNet
#  prototype sit at data/ in the repo root; TDC downloads land under
#  training/data/. Covering only one path is exactly how 22,000 lines of
#  CSV once got committed by accident.
data/raw/*
data/processed/*
data/pretrain/*
data/interim/*
data/cache/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/processed/.gitkeep
!data/pretrain/.gitkeep
training/data/raw/*
training/data/processed/*
training/data/pretrain/*
training/data/cache/*
!training/data/raw/.gitkeep
!training/data/processed/.gitkeep
!training/data/pretrain/.gitkeep

# Generated metrics and figures. Every number in here is reproducible with
# `just results`, which is the point -- no figure in the report is hand-copied, so
# committing a snapshot would create a second source of truth that drifts.
#
# When a specific number needs to be PRESERVED as evidence for an increment, it is
# copied into docs/evidence/<increment>/ deliberately, where it is un-ignored and
# dated. Evidence is a decision, not a side effect of having run something.
/results/

# The compiled report. `just report` rebuilds it from docs/report/main.typ in
# seconds, and the .typ source is the artefact under review. Committing the PDF
# would mean every edit produces a binary diff nobody can read, and a reviewer
# could never tell whether the checked-in PDF was built from the checked-in
# source. The submitted copy is a release artefact, not a tracked file.
docs/report/*.pdf
docs/report/page*.png

# Bulk dataset and archive formats -- never committed from any location.
# Small golden-vector fixtures are the deliberate exception, because CI
# must be able to verify feature parity without a download.
*.sdf
*.smi
*.csv.gz
*.tsv.gz
*.parquet
*.npz
!fixtures/**

# --- Model artifacts (large binaries -- ship via GitHub Releases) ---
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.onnx
serving/models/*
!serving/models/.gitkeep
# EXCEPTION: the tiny spike artefact is committed so CI can prove the
# ONNX round-trip without a full training run.
!fixtures/spike_tiny_gin.onnx

# --- Experiment tracking / logs ---
*.log
wandb/
mlruns/
lightning_logs/
runs/

# --- Docker ---
*.pid

# --- Diagram tool scratch files (export the PNG/SVG, commit that) ---
*.mdj.bak
*.uxf~

# --- IDE ---
.vscode/
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp

# --- OS ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Testing / coverage ---
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
tarpaulin-report.html
lcov.info

# =============================================================
#  MARKDOWN VISIBILITY -- deliberate decision
# =============================================================
#  Two tiers, and the distinction is what gets graded.
#
#  PUBLISHED (tracked):  docs/** -- the SRS, design document, test
#  plan, traceability matrix, ADRs, diagram specifications, weekly
#  journal. These are deliverables. They belong in version control
#  so their history is evidence: an examiner can see that ADR-03
#  was written before the model, not reverse-engineered after it.
#
#  PRIVATE (ignored):    /*.md at the repo root -- research.md,
#  method.md, requirements.md, implementation.md, MIGRATION.md.
#  These are working notes. They are where thinking happens, they
#  contradict themselves in places, and they are submitted as
#  finished documents rather than as a directory listing.
#
#  The pattern is `/*.md`, NOT `*.md`. The leading slash anchors it
#  to the root: without it, git ignores markdown at every depth and
#  docs/ silently vanishes -- which is a genuinely confusing bug,
#  because `git status` reports nothing at all rather than an error.
#
#  README.md is re-included because it is the repository's front
#  door and must be visible on the hosting page. START-HERE.md is
#  re-included because it is a deliverable in its own right -- the
#  week-by-week execution guide -- and it is useless to anyone who
#  clones the repository if it is not in the repository.
/*.md
!README.md
!START-HERE.md

# Evidence artefacts survive the bulk-format rules above. A test
# log or a coverage report committed under docs/evidence/ is there
# on purpose -- it is the proof behind a number in the report, and
# regenerating it months later on different hardware would produce
# a different number. See docs/evidence/README.md.
!docs/evidence/**
